From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
Subject: [PATCH] SPARC64: give the CPU node the I-cache's line size and size

4cbc339 ("Create extra CPU properties required by OpenSolaris kernel")
set icache-line-size and icache-size from the E-cache fields of the CPU
definition, so an UltraSPARC IIi reported a 1 MB instruction cache with
64-byte lines instead of 16 KB with 32-byte lines.

64-bit Solaris 9 checks the cache geometry in startup_modules() and
stopped with

  panic[cpu0]/thread=140a000: VAC too big!

once it got that far. Use the I-cache fields.
---
 arch/sparc64/openbios.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/sparc64/openbios.c b/arch/sparc64/openbios.c
index aa774c4..55bb3bb 100644
--- a/arch/sparc64/openbios.c
+++ b/arch/sparc64/openbios.c
@@ -374,12 +374,12 @@ static void cpu_generic_init(const struct cpudef *cpu, uint32_t clock_frequency)
     push_str("icache-associativity");
     fword("property");
 
-    PUSH(cpu->ecache_line_size);
+    PUSH(cpu->icache_line_size);
     fword("encode-int");
     push_str("icache-line-size");
     fword("property");
 
-    PUSH(cpu->ecache_size);
+    PUSH(cpu->icache_size);
     fword("encode-int");
     push_str("icache-size");
     fword("property");
